  <div class="container">

    <header>
      <span class="badge">A2 / Pre-Intermediate • Unit 2B</span>
      <h1>That's me in the picture!</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Memories, Photographs, Prepositions (at / in / on) & Past Continuous</p>
    </header>

    <!-- 1. WARM-UP -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>1. Warm-Up: Photos & Memories</h2>
      <div class="qa-item">
        <strong>1.</strong> Do you prefer taking photos of places and landscapes or taking pictures of people and friends?
      </div>
      <div class="qa-item">
        <strong>2.</strong> How often do you look through old photos on your phone or in printed albums?
      </div>
      <div class="qa-item">
        <strong>3.</strong> Do you have a favorite photo of yourself from your childhood or youth? What was happening in that picture?
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. READING -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>2. Reading: The Story Behind the Photo</h2>
      <div class="text-block">
        <p>In 1972, Jane Rangely was in her early twenties, living and working in London for an advertising agency. That summer, while on holiday with her parents in the south of France, she met a young Frenchman named Christian in a nightclub. They fell in love immediately. When Jane returned to London, she decided to find a job in Paris. She found work as a bilingual secretary, and Christian was studying medicine at university.</p>
        <p>On Sundays, they frequently went for walks around Paris. One autumn day, while walking in the botanical gardens, they paused because a noise came from a tree. A small bird was attacking an owl. While they were looking up, Jane noticed a man with a camera taking photographs of them.</p>
        <p>A year later, a friend in London recognized Jane in a published photography magazine. The photographer was Henri Cartier-Bresson, one of the most famous photographers in history. Jane contacted him, and he generously sent her a signed copy of the photograph. It captured a peaceful, romantic period of her youth that she still remembers warmly.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="qa-item">
        <strong>Comprehension Questions:</strong>
        <ol style="margin-left: 20px; margin-top: 8px;">
          <li>Where was Jane living and working before moving to Paris?</li>
          <li>What were Jane and Christian doing when the photo was taken?</li>
          <li>Why did they stop walking in the botanical gardens?</li>
          <li>How did Jane find out that Henri Cartier-Bresson had taken their photo?</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. PREPOSITIONS OF TIME & PLACE -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>3. Vocabulary: Prepositions (at, in, on)</h2>
      <div class="grammar-rule">
        <strong>Rule of thumb:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>IN:</strong> Years, months, seasons, cities, countries, enclosed spaces (in 1972, in Paris, in the garden).</li>
          <li><strong>ON:</strong> Days of the week, dates, islands, surfaces, public transport (on Sunday, on the beach, on the bus).</li>
          <li><strong>AT:</strong> Specific points, clock times, buildings/events (at 7:00, at university, at a party, at work).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="exercise-box" id="ex-prepositions">
        <div class="exercise-item">
          1. Jane met Christian <input type="text" data-ans="in" style="width: 70px;"> the south of France.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          2. They often went for romantic walks <input type="text" data-ans="on" style="width: 70px;"> Sundays.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          3. Christian was studying medicine <input type="text" data-ans="at" style="width: 70px;"> university.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          4. She was living <input type="text" data-ans="in" style="width: 70px;"> London when she got the letter.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          5. They were standing <input type="text" data-ans="in" style="width: 70px;"> the botanical gardens.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          6. Cartier-Bresson was waiting <input type="text" data-ans="at" style="width: 70px;"> the corner with his camera.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="btn-row">
        <button onclick="checkAnswers('ex-prepositions')">Check Answers</button>
        <button class="secondary" onclick="resetAnswers('ex-prepositions')">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. GRAMMAR: PAST CONTINUOUS VS PAST SIMPLE -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>4. Grammar: Past Continuous vs Past Simple</h2>
      <div class="grammar-rule">
        <strong>Form:</strong> was / were + verb-ing (I was working / They were walking).
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Past Continuous:</strong> Describes a longer background action in progress in the past.</li>
          <li><strong>Past Simple:</strong> Describes a shorter, completed action that interrupted the background action.</li>
          <li><em>Example:</em> We <strong>were walking</strong> in the park when it <strong>started</strong> to rain.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="exercise-box" id="ex-grammar">
        <div class="exercise-item">
          1. While Jane and Christian (walk) <input type="text" data-ans="were walking" style="width: 140px;">, they heard a noise.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          2. The photographer took a picture while they (look) <input type="text" data-ans="were looking" style="width: 140px;"> at the birds.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          3. It (rain) <input type="text" data-ans="was raining" style="width: 140px;"> when I left the house this morning.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          4. I was reading a magazine when my phone suddenly (ring) <input type="text" data-ans="rang" style="width: 100px;">.
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="exercise-item">
          5. What (you / do) <input type="text" data-ans="were you doing" style="width: 150px;"> when you saw the accident?
          <span class="status-msg"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="btn-row">
        <button onclick="checkAnswers('ex-grammar')">Check Answers</button>
        <button class="secondary" onclick="resetAnswers('ex-grammar')">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. SPEAKING -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>5. Speaking Task: Describe a Photo</h2>
